      {q:"35. HOTS: If sec θ + tan θ = p, prove that sec θ − tan θ = 1/p, wherever defined.",a:"Since sec²θ−tan²θ=1, (sec θ+tan θ)(sec θ−tan θ)=1. Given sec θ+tan θ=p, so p(sec θ−tan θ)=1. Therefore sec θ−tan θ=1/p.",type:"Long"}
